{
  "version": "0.1",
  "title": "From Emotion to Better Decisions",
  "subtitle": "Feel, Understand, Think, Then Act.",
  "note": "Emotions are signals, not decisions.",
  "style": "mindful",
  "shape": "rounded",
  "layout": {
    "type": "poster",
    "columns": 20
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "poster-card",
      "id": "fast-thinking",
      "span": 8,
      "tone": "rose",
      "title": "System 1 – Fast Thinking",
      "subtitle": "Automatic · Intuitive · Emotional · Effortless",
      "icon": "brain",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Quick, automatic reactions"
        },
        {
          "text": "Driven by emotion and past experience"
        },
        {
          "lead": "Great for:",
          "text": "danger, simple choices, familiar situations"
        },
        {
          "lead": "Risk:",
          "text": "biases, overreactions, short-sighted decisions"
        }
      ],
      "quote": "Helpful for speed. Not always reliable for complex problems."
    },
    {
      "type": "poster-card",
      "id": "slow-thinking",
      "span": 8,
      "tone": "blue",
      "title": "System 2 – Slow Thinking",
      "subtitle": "Deliberate · Analytical · Logical · Effortful",
      "icon": "brain",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Slower, more deliberate processing"
        },
        {
          "text": "Uses logic, analysis, and reasoning"
        },
        {
          "lead": "Great for:",
          "text": "complex problems, important decisions, novel situations"
        },
        {
          "lead": "Requires:",
          "text": "attention and mental effort"
        },
        {
          "lead": "Benefit:",
          "text": "more thoughtful, better long-term outcomes"
        }
      ],
      "quote": "Slower, but usually leads to better decisions."
    },
    {
      "type": "poster-insight",
      "id": "key-idea",
      "span": 4,
      "title": "The Key Idea",
      "icon": "lightbulb",
      "lead": "Emotional response typically won’t help you solve the problem.",
      "paragraphs": [
        "It’s often System 1 — fast, automatic, and reactive.",
        "When there’s a problem question, try to engage System 2 — slow, deliberate, and analytical."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "poster-flow",
      "id": "typical-flow",
      "span": 20,
      "title": "A Typical Flow",
      "subtitle": "What often happens vs. what can make a difference.",
      "lanes": [
        {
          "label": "The Usual (Reaction)",
          "tone": "rose",
          "stages": [
            {
              "icon": "bolt",
              "label": "Trigger",
              "detail": "Something happens"
            },
            {
              "icon": "mood_bad",
              "label": "Emotional response",
              "detail": "E.g., anger, anxiety"
            },
            {
              "icon": "directions_run",
              "label": "Immediate action",
              "detail": "Reaction"
            },
            {
              "icon": "help",
              "label": "Possible regret",
              "detail": "Or suboptimal outcome"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "A Better Approach (Responsive)",
          "tone": "mint",
          "stages": [
            {
              "icon": "bolt",
              "label": "Trigger",
              "detail": "Something happens"
            },
            {
              "icon": "sentiment_satisfied",
              "label": "Notice emotion",
              "detail": "A signal, not a decision"
            },
            {
              "icon": "pause",
              "label": "Pause",
              "detail": "Create space"
            },
            {
              "icon": "search",
              "label": "Frame the problem",
              "detail": "What’s actually going on?"
            },
            {
              "icon": "list",
              "label": "Explore options",
              "detail": "Evidence and trade-offs"
            },
            {
              "icon": "check",
              "label": "Take action",
              "detail": "Choose the best next step"
            },
            {
              "icon": "bar_chart",
              "label": "Better outcome",
              "detail": "Learn and adjust"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "poster-example",
      "id": "real-world-example",
      "span": 9,
      "title": "Real-World Example",
      "subtitle": "A colleague criticizes your proposal.",
      "columns": [
        {
          "title": "System 1 Reaction",
          "tone": "rose",
          "quote": "They just don’t understand.",
          "points": [
            "Feel defensive or angry",
            "Immediately argue back",
            "Relationship may suffer",
            "Miss useful feedback"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "System 2 Response",
          "tone": "blue",
          "quote": "What are they really concerned about?",
          "points": [
            "Notice the emotion",
            "Clarify the real issue",
            "Ask questions, gather evidence",
            "Adjust, explain, or decide not to change",
            "Better decision and stronger outcome"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "poster-steps",
      "id": "practical-framework",
      "span": 7,
      "title": "A Practical Framework",
      "subtitle": "When you notice a strong emotional response.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "What am I feeling?",
          "detail": "Name the emotion (angry, anxious, frustrated)."
        },
        {
          "title": "What is it telling me?",
          "detail": "What value, goal, or boundary might be affected?"
        },
        {
          "title": "What can I control?",
          "detail": "Focus on what is within my influence."
        },
        {
          "title": "What are my options?",
          "detail": "Generate and evaluate possible actions."
        },
        {
          "title": "Take the smallest useful action.",
          "detail": "Do one thing. Then observe and learn."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "poster-takeaways",
      "id": "key-takeaways",
      "span": 4,
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        {
          "icon": "brain",
          "text": "Emotion is a signal, not a decision."
        },
        {
          "icon": "pause",
          "text": "Pause creates choice."
        },
        {
          "icon": "settings",
          "text": "Use System 2 for problem-solving."
        },
        {
          "icon": "target",
          "text": "Focus on action, not just on feelings."
        },
        {
          "icon": "eco",
          "text": "If nothing is controllable, accept, let go, and redirect attention."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "poster-banner",
      "id": "closing",
      "span": 20,
      "icon": "flag",
      "title": "A Calmer Mind. Better Decisions. A Better You.",
      "text": "Feel it. Learn from it. Think about it. Do something useful.",
      "quote": "You can’t always control what happens. But you can choose how you think, and what you do next."
    }
  ]
}
